# Beads + beadfinder

This repo uses **bd (Beads)** for multi-session work. Do not use markdown TODOs or GitHub issues for that work.

Skill: `beadfinder`. Companions: `grill`, `research`, `to-spec`, `to-tickets`, `implement`, `review`. Optional: `beadfinder-debug`.
Primary agent: `wayfinder`. Workers: `architect`, `implementer`, `reviewer`, `product`.
OMP hooks: `.omp/extensions/beadfinder`. OpenCode plugin: `.opencode/plugins/beadfinder.ts`.

```bash
bd prime
bd ready --parent <slice-id> --label implementation --unassigned --json
bd update <id> --claim --json
scripts/review-submit.sh <id>              # implementer: done -> review queue
bd close <id> --reason "Review PASS: quality 9/10, correctness 8/10, pillars 9/10. <gist>"   # reviewer only, on pass
```

Claim before work. One non-research ticket per session. HITL stays in the wayfinder session. Build beads close only via a passing review: the implementer submits with `scripts/review-submit.sh` (in the installed beadfinder skill's scripts/ directory), the reviewer scores quality/correctness/pillars 1–10 (pass = all ≥ 8, evidence mandatory) or fails it back — loop until pass.

Beads on disk is the source of truth for ticket status. Re-run `bd show <id> --json` before claiming or closing. Do not trust an older chat line that says a bead is still open. The store is `.beads/`, not `beads/`.
